    "blocks_7tcEyN": {
      "type": "_blocks",
      "blocks": {
        "ai_gen_block_fb81b45_XmXidb": {
          "type": "editorial--content",
          "settings": {
            "desktop_width_percent": 100,
            "max_width": 1200,
            "section_padding": 20,
            "background_color": "#f9f6f1",
            "heading": "<p>DAY THREE, STILL IN IT: ADDICTION (inspired by Baccarat Rouge 540)</p>",
            "heading_size": 48,
            "heading_color": "#000000",
            "heading_spacing": 10,
            "box_color": "#8b1d22",
            "box_radius": 25,
            "box_padding": 40,
            "box_spacing": 10,
            "box_paragraph_1": "<p>By day three you are running on festival energy and strong coffee. Sleep happened. The schedule is still packed. You are not slowing down. Addiction is the scent for exactly this. Inspired by Baccarat Rouge 540, it opens with jasmine and saffron and settles into amber and cedar with a warmth that the desert heat takes to right away.</p>",
            "box_paragraph_2": "<p>The kind of niche fragrance that US buyers come back to because it smells like something that should cost significantly more. On day three, still being there is already the win. Smelling like this while being there is everything.</p>",
            "box_paragraph_3": "",
            "box_text_color": "#ffffff",
            "box_text_size": 22,
            "box_text_line_height": 1.6,
            "paragraph_spacing": 25,
            "subheading": "",
            "subheading_size": 50,
            "subheading_color": "#000000",
            "subheading_spacing": 10,
